{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q413586","formula":"C₂₁H₂₁N","hill":"C21H21N","elements":["H","C","N"],"composition":{"C":21.0,"H":21.0,"N":1.0},"names":{"en":"Naftifine","ru":"Naftin","uk":"Нафтифін"},"descriptions":{"en":"Naftifine hydrochloride (brand names include Exoderil and Naftin) is an allylamine antifungal drug for the topical treatment of tinea pedis, tinea cruris, and tinea corporis (topical fungal infections). Naftifine was invented at the Sandoz Research Institute in Vienna, Austria. It was the first successful antifungal medication of the allylamine class.","ru":"Нафтифи́н — противогрибковое средство для наружного применения, относящееся к классу аллиламинов. Открыт в 1974 году компанией Sandoz Research Institute в Вене, Австрия. Было установлено, что нафтифин борется с большим количеством значимых грибков.","uk":"Нафтифін — синтетичний протигрибковий препарат, що належить до групи аліламінів для місцевого застосування."},"fame":25,"pubchemCid":47641,"mass":287.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN(C/C=C/C1=CC=CC=C1)CC2=CC=CC3=CC=CC=C32","inchikey":"OZGNYLLQHRPOBR-DHZHZOJOSA-N","iupac":"(E)-N-methyl-N-(naphthalen-1-ylmethyl)-3-phenylprop-2-en-1-amine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"47641","atoms":43,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.543,"y":2.025,"z":-0.939,"el":"N"},{"x":0.723,"y":1.353,"z":0.347,"el":"C"},{"x":2.104,"y":0.796,"z":0.505,"el":"C"},{"x":2.433,"y":-0.508,"z":0.098,"el":"C"},{"x":3.757,"y":-0.975,"z":0.275,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.832,"y":2.502,"z":-1.079,"el":"C"},{"x":3.067,"y":1.626,"z":1.079,"el":"C"},{"x":1.485,"y":3.136,"z":-1.071,"el":"C"},{"x":1.476,"y":-1.357,"z":-0.482,"el":"C"},{"x":4.713,"y":-0.125,"z":0.854,"el":"C"},{"x":4.369,"y":1.167,"z":1.253,"el":"C"},{"x":4.086,"y":-2.278,"z":-0.133,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.82,"y":1.381,"z":-0.9